        {
            Title = "Period Close and Year-End",
            Slug = "gl-period-close",
            Summary = "Soft close, hard close and reopen for a period, and what the year-end close does with the retained-earnings roll",
            ContentType = TrainingContentType.Article,
            EstimatedMinutes = 5,
            IsPublished = true,
            SortOrder = 7,
            AppRoutes = """["/accounting/period-close"]""",
            Tags = """["accounting","general-ledger","period-close","year-end"]""",
            ContentJson = """{"body":"## Period Close and Year-End\n\nThe **Period Close** page lists each fiscal year with its periods — usually twelve months — and a status chip on every one. Closing a period is how you tell the ledger *these numbers are done*, so a late bill or a backdated payment cannot quietly change a month you have already reported.\n\n### The three period states\n\n- **Open** — anything can post into it.\n- **Soft-closed** — nothing can post into it, but you can **Reopen** it. This is the normal month-end state: close the month, send the reports, and reopen only if the accountant finds something.\n- **Hard-closed** — nothing can post, and it cannot be reopened. The row shows **Locked**. Use it once the month has been reported outside the company or the year is done.\n\nFrom an Open period the actions are **Soft-close** and **Hard-close**. From Soft-closed they are **Reopen** and **Hard-close**. A Hard-closed period offers nothing.\n\n### A month-end routine\n\n1. Finish the operational work: invoices sent, bills entered, payments applied, payroll run.\n2. Run the **Bank Reconciliation** for each cash account and finalize it.\n3. Post the manual entries — accruals, depreciation, prepaid amortization.\n4. Check the **Trial Balance** balances and the **Profit & Loss** looks like the month you had.\n5. **Soft-close** the period.\n6. Send the reports. If something comes back, reopen, fix, soft-close again.\n7. Once the month is final, **Hard-close** it.\n\n### Year-end: Close year (RE roll)\n\nWhile a fiscal year is Open, its header shows **Close year (RE roll)**. This does two things at once, and Forge asks you to confirm because neither can be undone:\n\n1. It posts the **retained-earnings roll**: every income and expense account is zeroed out and the net result for the year is moved into retained earnings, so the new year starts its Profit & Loss from nothing while the Balance Sheet carries the accumulated result forward.\n2. It **hard-closes every period** in the year.\n\nDo it only after the accountant has signed off on the year, all twelve months are at least soft-closed, and the year-end adjustments are posted. Once the year is closed, adjustments for that year have to be posted as entries dated in the new year.\n\n### What to do if a period will not close\n\nA soft close always goes through. A **hard close** is permanent, so Forge first checks that the books are clean as of the period end: goods received but not yet billed must tie between the ledger and receiving, and the AR and AP aging reports must tie to their control accounts. If any of those is off, the page shows an error naming the check and the difference; fix it (usually a missing bill or an unapplied payment) and try again.\n\nClosing also carries any auto-reversing accruals into the first day of the next period, so the next period has to exist before you close this one. If it does not, the error says so — set up the next period and close again.","sections":[]}"""
