            Tags = """["accounting","general-ledger","budgets"]""",
            ContentJson = """{"body":"## Budgets\n\nThe **Budgets** page gives every income and expense account a budget for a fiscal year and then shows how actual postings compare. It has a year stepper at the top and two tabs.\n\n### Budget Entry\n\nStep to the year you are budgeting. The **Budget Entry** tab lists every active income and expense account with a **Budget Amount** box. Enter the amount for the full year and click **Save**. Nothing is stored until you save, and you can come back and change amounts at any time — budgets are not locked by period close.\n\nAccounts that are not income or expense do not appear; budgets are about the Profit & Loss, not the Balance Sheet. If the tab says there are no accounts to budget, add income and expense accounts on the Chart of Accounts first.\n\nIf you ran the costing **Quick start** with its ledger toggle on, the overhead lines it created already have budget amounts here.\n\n### Budget vs Actual\n\nThe **Budget vs Actual** tab adds a **Period** selector — a month of the chosen year or the full year — and shows one row per account with **Budget**, **Actual**, **Variance** and **Variance %**, plus a total row. Actual is what the ledger posted for the period. Variance is budget minus actual, so a positive variance on an expense account means you spent less than planned, and on an income account means you earned less than planned; the color follows the sign, not whether the news is good.\n\nUse it at month end alongside the Profit & Loss: the statement tells you what happened, this tab tells you how far it is from what you expected.","sections":[]}"""
